tion). Bit 7 (fuel unit) is no longer skipped: with unit \"L\" or no unit the bit 8 value goes to `fuel` (liters), with any other unit it goes to `fuelLevel` (percentage).\n- Learned: the existing real sample (`...|00000000000041DF;...;P;80;69$`) has unit \"P\", so it now decodes to `fuelLevel` 80 instead of `fuel` 80.\n- Left: there is no real device sample with bits 15 to 38. The test for these bits uses a synthetic CAN block (mask `0000007FFFFFFFFF`) on top of a real event block. Replace it with a real message when one is available.\nEOF","description":"Append entry to harness log"}}}
